1. About This License

The Try Again License governs use of the software, documentation, frameworks, methodologies, prompts, templates, workflows, and related materials made available by the licensor under this license.

This license is based on a simple principle:

If “try again” is an acceptable recovery strategy, Community use likely applies.
If “try again” is not an acceptable recovery strategy, Commercial use likely applies.

Some systems can safely recover from mistakes by retrying, regenerating, rewriting, rerunning, rolling back, or human review. Other systems cannot. When mistakes are cheap, reversible, and low-consequence, broad community use is encouraged. When mistakes can create financial loss, legal exposure, medical harm, physical harm, regulatory violation, material operational disruption, reputational harm, military consequences, institutional harm, or large-scale societal consequences, a commercial license is required.

This license creates three categories of use:

1. Community Use
    Free use for low-consequence, retry-safe systems.
1. Growth / Limited Commercial Use
    Free or low-friction use until meaningful commercial scale, after which a commercial license is required.
1. Full Commercial Use
    Commercial license required from day one for high-consequence systems.

This license is not an open-source license as defined by the Open Source Initiative because it restricts certain commercial, field-specific, and high-consequence uses.

⸻

